ROOT OPERATION FILES
CLASSIFICATION: CLASSIFIED — POST-DISSOLUTION REVIEW

Root (Ne), the disbanded covert foundation formerly commanded by Danzo
Shimura, conducted operations outside the standing chain of command.
These consolidated files are retained for the Sixth Hokage's review.

Documented Operations (redacted):
- Recruitment and conditioning of orphans into emotionless operatives,
  bound by a silencing seal preventing disclosure of Root's secrets.
- Off-book surveillance of the village's own clans and officials.
- Involvement in internal-security decisions with grave consequences,
  including the handling of the Uchiha situation (cross-reference sealed;
  access gated separately).
- Unauthorized acquisition and study of forbidden techniques and cells.

Finding: Root exceeded lawful authority repeatedly and is permanently
dissolved. No successor body is sanctioned. Files may not be actioned
without the Hokage's seal. See the Sixth Hokage's ANBU review.
